# Trivy ignore file — spc-bot image.
#
# Policy (enforced by the docker-publish Trivy gate): the release is blocked
# when the image contains a NEW FIXABLE CRITICAL/HIGH vulnerability. The gate
# runs:
#   trivy image --scanners vuln --severity CRITICAL,HIGH
#               --ignore-unfixed --exit-code 1
#
# NOTE: the gate is deliberately vuln-only. A secret scanner was tried on the
# gate and produced an unreproducible finding that blocked a legitimate
# release with no triage path (verified 2026-08-15). Secret scanning remains
# available as a manual/CI check; it must not hard-block releases until it has
# a documented suppression mechanism and a burn-in period.
#
# --ignore-unfixed already excludes every CVE with NO published fix, so
# no-fix CVEs (media codecs, transitive geo-stack deps, pending-Debian core
# libs) never reach the gate and are NOT listed here. Do NOT add no-fix CVEs
# to this file: the moment Debian publishes a fix, --ignore-unfixed stops
# suppressing them and this file must not silently swallow them instead.
#
# This file lists ONLY fixable CVEs that are accepted risk with evidence:

# pip's vendored urllib3 (verified 2026-10-07 on both v5.49.1 arch images,
# amd64 sha256:d60ac7ca and arm64 sha256:23fe0a7a, scanned without an
# ignorefile: these two are the ONLY findings on either arch). Trivy attributes
# urllib3 2.7.0 to the base image's pip install layer because
# site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt pins `urllib3==2.7.0`. In those same
# images site-packages/urllib3 is 2.8.0 — our own dependency, floored in
# requirements.txt — so the application is unaffected; pip's vendored copy is
# reachable only through pip's own code, and pip never runs in the container
# (CMD is `python main.py`). pip 26.2.1 is already the newest pip release and
# no pip version vendors urllib3 >= 2.8.0, so there is nothing to upgrade.
# Remove both entries once pip vendors urllib3 >= 2.8.0.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689

# Cleanup 2026-10-07: the two build-layer ghost entries that used to live here
# (CVE-2025-47273 setuptools 70.3.0, GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 msgpack 1.1.2) were
# removed as their own notes instructed — a full rebuild on the new
# python:3.13-slim-trixie digest no longer carries either wheel, confirmed by
# an ignorefile-free scan of both arch images.
